---
description: Check dependencies for known CVEs and fix them safely (am-i-cooked). Use when asked "am i cooked", about vulnerable dependencies, new CVEs, or auditing a lockfile.
alwaysApply: false
---

Install once: `npx skills add noushiFlex/am-i-cooked -a cursor` (installs to `.agents/skills/am-i-cooked`).

To check the project, run `node .agents/skills/am-i-cooked/scripts/scan.mjs .` and follow `.agents/skills/am-i-cooked/SKILL.md`, then `FIXING.md` if the user agrees to fix.

Rules that always apply:
- Facts come from the scanner output only. Never invent a CVE id, CVSS score or fixed version.
- Never say "safe" when the verdict is `unknown`, when the scan failed, or before re-scanning after a change.
- Ask before changing anything. Work on a `fix/cves-<date>` branch, one safe upgrade at a time, run the tests after each.
- Confirm every fix with `scan.mjs . --baseline=before.json`.
- Never push, open a PR, edit `.cookedignore`, or run `npm audit fix --force` without explicit approval.
